  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "📦 VDocs – Release Notes\n🚀 Version: 2026.1.1\n\nThis release introduces major improvements to Header and Footer processing, expanding VDocs’ document layout capabilities and making complex Word documents easier to generate and manipulate programmatically.\n\n✨ What’s New\n🧾 Enhanced Header and Footer Mapping\n\n - Revised DOM ↔ Word XML mapping for headers and footers to improve correctness and stability.\n\n - Improved alignment with WordprocessingML structure (hdr, ftr, section-level references).\n\n - Safer XML generation to ensure documents open reliably in Microsoft Word.\n\n🔁 Multi Header and Footer Support\n\n - Added support for multiple headers and footers within a single document, including:\n\n   - Different First Page headers/footers\n\n   - Odd and Even page headers/footers\n\n   - Section-specific header/footer definitions\n\n - Each header/footer is now handled as an independent part with its own XML and relationship scope.\n\n🔗 Improved Relationship Handling\n\n - Automatic creation and management of header/footer relationship parts (headerX.xml.rels, footerX.xml.rels).\n\n - Correct rId assignment and section references during reverse mapping.\n\n - Better isolation of media and drawing relationships per header/footer part.\n\n🛠 Improvements\n\n - More robust XML generation for header/footer content, including:\n\n   - Paragraphs\n\n   - Tables\n\n   - Images\n\n - Reduced risk of Word compatibility issues caused by invalid or incomplete XML.\n\n - Cleaner internal APIs to support future extensions (e.g., advanced layout rules).\n\n🧩 Backward Compatibility\n\n - Existing documents and mappings remain compatible.\n\n - No breaking changes to public APIs.\n\n📌 Recommended For\n\nDevelopers generating or transforming Word documents that require:\n\n - Section-aware layouts\n\n - Different headers/footers per page type\n\n - Full control over document structure without Word automation",
  "requireLicenseAcceptance": true,
  "title": "VDocs - Word Document Framework",
